PurchaseLossEventBody[0]="The transport received a stop order at an ADVENT checkpoint. To break pursuit, the courier left several unmarked crates at a temporary cache, but a patrol seized them before the recovery team arrived."
PurchaseLossEventBody[1]="A packer at the relay warehouse misclassified crates bearing similar marks. The broker is tracing the missing goods, but they could not be included in this delivery."
PurchaseLossEventBody[2]="An ADVENT surveillance drone followed the transport. The driver escaped through the ruins, but several damaged packages had to be abandoned before the vehicle could clear the cordon."
PurchaseLossEventBody[3]="The final handoff point was at risk of exposure, forcing the shipment onto several improvised routes. The cargo assigned to one courier who went silent never reached the destination."
PurchaseLossEventBody[4]="Heavy rain flooded part of the underground route. The recovery team extracted the vehicle and personnel first, but some submerged cargo was no longer usable."
PurchaseLossEventBody[5]="The relay cipher was retired earlier than scheduled, preventing authentication at the final cache. Unable to rule out tracking tags, the contact burned part of the shipment on site."
PurchaseLossEventBody[6]="The inside contact managing the order route was arrested without warning. To contain the breach, the broker abandoned the storehouse under that contact's control along with part of the order."
PurchaseLossEventBody[7]="The forged manifest did not match the actual cargo weight and drew a checkpoint inspector's attention. The courier separated several crates as civilian freight but could not recover them later."
PurchaseLossEventBody[8]="A road closure forced the cargo onto a small boat, which took fire during the crossing. The crew escaped, but packages contaminated by seawater had to be discarded."
PurchaseLossEventBody[9]="A refugee shelter near the route came under attack. The local Resistance diverted part of the cargo to evacuate the wounded, and the broker reported that the decision prevented further loss of life."
PurchaseLossEventBody[10]="A jammer failure caused the safe window at the unattended handoff point to expire. By the time the courier arrived, unknown scavengers had already taken part of the cache."
PurchaseLossEventBody[11]="An aging generator overheated and started a fire in the temporary warehouse. Guards contained the blaze, but some of the order stacked near the entrance could not be recovered."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[0]="The supplier packing the order appears to have loaded an extra crate with the same markings. The broker decided that recovering it would expose more of the route than simply delivering it to XCOM."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[1]="The broker added part of a reserve stockpile for a trusted customer with a clean transaction record. Only the original order quantity appears in the official ledger."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[2]="A supplier had to empty a cache before it was closed. There was no safe opportunity to arrange another shipment, so the remaining stock was added to this delivery."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[3]="Two isolated relay cells processed copies of the same order, producing duplicate crates. Neither cell was willing to reopen its route for collection, so the excess was assigned to XCOM."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[4]="An ADVENT sweep dismantled a rival dealer's route, and ownerless cargo reached the same cache. Its specifications matched the order, so the broker included it in the delivery."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[5]="A supplier settled an old debt to the broker with goods. Rather than create another ledger entry, the settlement was divided among the crates in this order."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[6]="The manufacturer's bundle size did not match the quantity notation on the order. Repacking was judged less secure than shipping the sealed bundles, leaving XCOM with the excess."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[7]="A local Resistance cell recently extracted by an XCOM operation surrendered part of its allocation. The extra cargo arrived with a short message saying that no repayment was necessary."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[8]="An anonymous supporter left matching goods at the relay station and disappeared. Inspection found no tracking device or hostile marker, so the donation was added to the order."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[9]="A captured ADVENT manifest exposed an unrecovered supply cache close to the delivery route. The transport team secured the extra stock before completing the handoff."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[10]="The courier had a small remainder from another transaction that was unsafe to store separately. With the broker's approval, the matching stock was consolidated into this delivery."
PurchaseBonusEventBody[11]="A crate with damaged outer packaging could no longer be sold as regular stock. Its contents were intact, and the supplier transferred all of it rather than pay to dispose of it."
SaleLossEventBody[0]="The handoff team lost its transport and forged papers while fleeing an ADVENT checkpoint. Replacement vehicles and a new route were paid for from the final settlement."
SaleLossEventBody[1]="Surveillance around the exchange point intensified without warning. Contacts spent part of the payment bribing checkpoint personnel and erasing the resulting communication records."
SaleLossEventBody[2]="The Resistance convoy carrying the goods was attacked on its return route. Both sides shared the emergency cost of recovering the survivors and remaining cargo, reducing the settlement."
SaleLossEventBody[3]="Final inspection found that some packaging had been damaged in transit. The buyer kept the transaction in place but refused full payment for the additional risk."
SaleLossEventBody[4]="The buyer's payment cache was compromised by an ADVENT investigation. Converting traceable resources into a safe settlement reduced the final amount."
SaleLossEventBody[5]="The local Resistance group changed commanders just before the handoff, and the new commander rejected the previous terms. Accepting a lower settlement caused less damage than canceling the exchange."
SaleLossEventBody[6]="An armed smuggling crew took control of the planned route and demanded passage fees. A firefight would have exposed the handoff point, so the contact paid from the transaction."
SaleLossEventBody[7]="A sudden storm delayed transport and required another cover vehicle and temporary storehouse. Both sides agreed to deduct the shared emergency expenses from the settlement."
SaleLossEventBody[8]="An ADVENT cargo scanner marked the handoff container. The contacts bought a same-sized decoy to create enough time to move the real goods, and its cost was deducted from the payment."
SaleLossEventBody[9]="The broker discovered that some of the buyer's resources carried obsolete marks linked to a monitored cache. The conversion loss from replacing them with safe resources reduced the final receipt."
SaleLossEventBody[10]="A relay error caused the buyer and courier to interpret the quoted figure as gross and net payment respectively. To avoid a confrontation, the exchange closed after actual transport costs were deducted."
SaleLossEventBody[11]="The Resistance team coming to collect the goods suffered heavy casualties. Both sides agreed to redirect part of the payment to treatment and evacuation of the survivors."
SaleBonusEventBody[0]="A local Resistance cell needed these goods sooner than expected. Rather than wait for another buyer, they paid a premium for immediate priority at the handoff."
SaleBonusEventBody[1]="The buyer's technician found the goods in better condition than the report suggested. An additional payment was approved to secure priority on future shipments from the same route."
SaleBonusEventBody[2]="The broker granted a trust bonus to a customer who has consistently met promised quantities and schedules. Several contacts contributed to the separate settlement."
SaleBonusEventBody[3]="Two Resistance groups competed for the same goods. The broker revised the terms at the handoff, and the final collection team paid more than the original offer."
SaleBonusEventBody[4]="The buyer secured unexpected donor funding. With XCOM's exchange already prepared and judged the safest option, part of the surplus budget was assigned as additional payment."
SaleBonusEventBody[5]="The goods matched the exact specifications of an operation already under way. The local Resistance shared part of the cost saved by avoiding a search for substitutes."
SaleBonusEventBody[6]="The broker consolidated several small buyers into one handoff. Reduced transport costs left a difference that returned to XCOM as additional revenue."
SaleBonusEventBody[7]="The handoff cleared surveillance and finished ahead of schedule. The buyer settled unused security and diversion funds as a performance bonus."
SaleBonusEventBody[8]="Production marks left on the goods revealed a clue to the movement of an ADVENT supply route. The buyer's intelligence staff added compensation for the unexpected value of the information."
SaleBonusEventBody[9]="The buyer requested first negotiation rights on similar goods in the future. The broker promised only priority contact and included its price in this settlement."
SaleBonusEventBody[10]="A local broadcast presented the acquired goods as proof of successful Resistance activity, increasing recruitment and donations. The organization returned part of the new resources to XCOM."
SaleBonusEventBody[11]="A defected ADVENT quartermaster verified the goods and their preservation. With the risk removed, the buyer authorized payment above the agreed price."
